WEBVTT

00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:14.500
What is that planet?!

00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:16.500
If that's not Earth,

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:19.000
where did you all come from?!

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:20.660
Our planet?

00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:23.370
That's obvious.

00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:24.580
Planet...

00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:25.870
...Astra.

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:37.660
What is this continent?

00:00:37.660 --> 00:00:39.160
Continent Carifa.

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:40.250
And this one?

00:00:40.250 --> 00:00:43.160
Continent Aria Sue.

00:00:43.160 --> 00:00:46.870
Like I thought, this is nothing
like the Earth I know...

00:00:46.870 --> 00:00:48.910
Astra and Earth.

00:00:48.910 --> 00:00:52.660
Our planet and yours are not the same.
That's the only possible conclusion.

00:00:52.660 --> 00:00:54.620
That makes no sense!

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:57.410
So there are people also living
on this "Earth" planet, too?

00:00:57.410 --> 00:00:58.870
Listen.

00:00:58.870 --> 00:01:01.910
This is my theory, but...

00:01:01.910 --> 00:01:03.700
Maybe Polina is a space alien?

00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:04.660
Are you an idiot?!

00:01:04.660 --> 00:01:06.790
No, I mean like, she's taking
on the form of a human!

00:01:06.790 --> 00:01:08.700
Shut up already, you broken robot!

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:12.120
Sorry Polina. His brain
is made of cream puffs.

00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:16.700
He's right. From your point of view,
I am from an alien planet...

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:19.660
Oh, don't cry, it's so easy
to make you cry.

00:01:19.660 --> 00:01:22.500
It's clear that we are all the same humans.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:23.870
We also speak the same language.

00:01:23.870 --> 00:01:27.540
But the difference in home
planets can't be ignored.

00:01:27.540 --> 00:01:31.870
I'm speaking English now,
but my mother tongue is Russian.

00:01:31.870 --> 00:01:33.330
"Russia." Have you heard of it?

00:01:33.330 --> 00:01:35.410
Hmm... No.

00:01:35.410 --> 00:01:38.910
It's a "country" right? I know.

00:01:38.910 --> 00:01:40.540
You know about Russia?!

00:01:40.540 --> 00:01:42.000
A "country"...

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:44.250
It's an outdated geopolitical designation.

00:01:44.250 --> 00:01:45.620
Those don't exist anymore.

00:01:45.620 --> 00:01:48.540
There are no countries...?

00:01:48.540 --> 00:01:50.160
The northern part of
the Aria Sue continent

00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:54.120
is where the Russian Empire was,
and it later became the Soviet Union.

00:01:54.120 --> 00:01:59.950
China was there, the small island next
to it is Japan. Below China is India...

00:01:59.950 --> 00:02:01.000
Wow.

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:03.500
--Old Era maps, I don't remember that at all.

00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:04.410
--Everything is out of place, but the
relative positions are somewhat correct.
--Old Era maps, I don't remember that at all.

00:02:04.410 --> 00:02:06.790
--Everything is out of place, but the
relative positions are somewhat correct.

00:02:06.790 --> 00:02:10.120
The difference is... time?

00:02:10.120 --> 00:02:15.700
It seems like comparing our histories
is the key to solving this.

00:02:17.870 --> 00:02:22.290
We then started discussing
the histories of our worlds.

00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:28.410
Let's see, Industrial Revolution,
First and Second World Wars, right?

00:02:28.410 --> 00:02:31.120
It seems pretty similar up to here.

00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:36.750
I'm surprised by how vague your knowledge is.
Don't they teach history in school?

00:02:36.750 --> 00:02:40.370
There are classes, but we don't
cover the Old Era much.

00:02:40.370 --> 00:02:43.830
I found it interesting so I read
some books on my own,

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:46.120
but there just aren't very many books
that cover this deeply.

00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:47.750
Not many books?

00:02:47.750 --> 00:02:52.500
In school we are taught to look towards
the future instead of dwelling on the past.

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:57.660
What...? Studying history
is the most important thing.

00:02:57.660 --> 00:03:03.450
Something feels... deliberate.
Like they're trying to hide history...

00:03:03.450 --> 00:03:07.910
And then there's the key turning
point after the Cold War.

00:03:07.910 --> 00:03:11.750
World War III, 1962.

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:15.580
World War III?! What is that?!

00:03:15.580 --> 00:03:18.660
1962 was the year of
the Cuban Missile Crisis!

00:03:18.660 --> 00:03:20.160
Cuban Missile Crisis?

00:03:20.160 --> 00:03:24.160
Cuba is the name of the country with
the base that got bombed, right?

00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:27.870
That was the trigger that lead to the war.

00:03:27.870 --> 00:03:30.790
Wait. In the history that I know
the base was not bombed

00:03:30.790 --> 00:03:33.290
and the war was averted!

00:03:33.290 --> 00:03:36.580
History branched off!
This is the juncture!

00:03:36.580 --> 00:03:39.790
A war happened after
the Cuban Missile Crisis...

00:03:39.790 --> 00:03:43.160
Oh, God... What is this...?

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:45.160
God?

00:03:45.160 --> 00:03:47.910
Polina, what is "God"?

00:03:50.450 --> 00:03:56.250
He doesn't know what "God" is?
No countries or religions?

00:03:56.250 --> 00:04:01.000
Tell me what happened
after that in your history.

00:04:02.410 --> 00:04:09.620
October 27th, 1962.
The USA and USSR entered into war.

00:04:09.620 --> 00:04:16.620
Nuclear missiles were used, sending
the world into an all-out nuclear war.

00:04:16.620 --> 00:04:19.660
The war itself lasted only two months,

00:04:19.660 --> 00:04:24.620
but half the population
of the world was lost.

00:04:24.620 --> 00:04:32.080
Humanity regretted its foolish actions
and vowed to rebuild a peaceful world.

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:36.660
1963, the United World Government
is formed. Countries are abolished.

00:04:36.660 --> 00:04:42.540
Also, the greatest wish of all people
was realized--the abolishment of guns.

00:04:42.540 --> 00:04:47.660
People overcame differences in race
and worked together to rebuild very quickly.

00:04:47.660 --> 00:04:52.790
Humanity was finally able
to create a peaceful world.

00:04:52.790 --> 00:04:57.160
This is nothing like what I know...
How did this happen?

00:04:57.160 --> 00:05:00.700
Or, in fact, did these things really happen?

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:08.200
Now it's your turn. Tell us, is it true
that your world never had WWIII?

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:09.250
Yes...

00:05:09.250 --> 00:05:13.790
It was far from peaceful,
but there was no global war.

00:05:13.790 --> 00:05:19.580
But a far greater threat emerged, one that
overwrote all other petty human conflicts.

00:05:19.580 --> 00:05:25.330
2049, an asteroid was discovered on a
collision course with Earth within eight years.

00:05:25.330 --> 00:05:26.910
An asteroid?!

00:05:26.910 --> 00:05:33.040
About 300km in diameter. It would have
killed all life on the planet if it struck.

00:05:33.040 --> 00:05:34.950
You have to be kidding!

00:05:34.950 --> 00:05:37.750
2057 already passed!

00:05:37.750 --> 00:05:40.040
We weren't hit by an asteroid!

00:05:40.040 --> 00:05:45.580
Let's hear her out. We already established
that her history is different from ours.

00:05:45.580 --> 00:05:51.370
There was only one solution--
to immigrate to a new planet.

00:05:51.370 --> 00:05:55.330
All of humanity, a selection of plants
and animals, historical relics...

00:05:55.330 --> 00:05:59.410
A plan was made to take as many things
as possible to a new planet.

00:05:59.410 --> 00:06:00.750
Planetary immigration?!

00:06:00.750 --> 00:06:03.290
There's no way you can
carry all of humanity!

00:06:03.290 --> 00:06:05.120
It's possible.

00:06:05.120 --> 00:06:07.540
With the artificial wormholes.

00:06:07.540 --> 00:06:10.620
Artificial... wormhole?

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:16.330
Could it be?!

00:06:16.330 --> 00:06:17.870
What's a wormhole?

00:06:17.870 --> 00:06:20.370
It's like a tunnel that goes
through time and space.

00:06:20.370 --> 00:06:23.040
Unlike spaceship faster-than-light travel,

00:06:23.040 --> 00:06:25.620
I've never heard that such
technology was already available.

00:06:25.620 --> 00:06:27.500
Wait, so maybe...!

00:06:27.500 --> 00:06:32.700
Yes, the thought crossed my mind
when you told me your story.

00:06:32.700 --> 00:06:36.330
The sphere of light could
have been a wormhole.

00:06:37.830 --> 00:06:41.540
At that time,
while working on that technology,

00:06:41.540 --> 00:06:45.410
we were scrambling to find
a good planet to move to.

00:06:45.410 --> 00:06:48.330
The Arc series of spaceships
was used precisely for that task.

00:06:48.330 --> 00:06:52.000
This is probably the <i>Arc XII</i>--
the one that was never used.

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:56.700
You already know what happened
to the <i>Arc VI</i>, which I was on.

00:06:56.700 --> 00:07:02.290
So you don't know what happened
after that? Did the exodus work?

00:07:02.290 --> 00:07:05.160
The exodus most likely...

00:07:05.160 --> 00:07:06.540
...finished successfully.

00:07:07.790 --> 00:07:09.290
I knew it.

00:07:09.290 --> 00:07:10.290
Yes.

00:07:10.290 --> 00:07:13.660
The planet that was chosen
was Planet Astra.

00:07:13.660 --> 00:07:17.500
You all are former Earthlings
who moved to Astra.

00:07:17.500 --> 00:07:18.330
What?!

00:07:18.330 --> 00:07:19.330
It can't be!

00:07:19.330 --> 00:07:21.830
There are still some things
that don't make sense,

00:07:21.830 --> 00:07:23.620
but that is the only logical conclusion.

00:07:23.620 --> 00:07:27.790
The exodus was completed,
and afterwards the asteroid struck Earth...

00:07:27.790 --> 00:07:29.950
So how is Earth now?!

00:07:31.450 --> 00:07:36.080
You said when the sphere swallowed you

00:07:36.080 --> 00:07:40.160
it spat you out above
a lifeless ice planet, right?

00:07:40.160 --> 00:07:44.700
Ice planet...? Yes! There was!

00:07:44.700 --> 00:07:45.910
Wait, so...

00:07:47.120 --> 00:07:49.910
That was Earth.

00:07:51.910 --> 00:07:57.040
The dust from the asteroid impact
blocked off the sun, causing an ice age...

00:07:57.040 --> 00:08:01.790
The sphere of light must have been
one of the gates used in the exodus.

00:08:01.790 --> 00:08:06.120
This <i>Arc XII </i>might have been parked
over the terminal above Earth

00:08:06.120 --> 00:08:11.660
and was knocked out into free orbit
due to the asteroid or something.

00:08:11.660 --> 00:08:13.370
So...

00:08:13.370 --> 00:08:19.000
All this time, we were travelling
from Earth to Astra.

00:08:21.750 --> 00:08:24.120
But the chronology doesn't make sense.

00:08:24.120 --> 00:08:30.580
The current year is 2063.
Assuming the exodus was complete in 2057,

00:08:30.580 --> 00:08:32.620
it's only been six years.

00:08:32.620 --> 00:08:39.250
No matter how similar to Earth Astra was,
it should haven take much longer to colonize it.

00:08:39.250 --> 00:08:42.580
Is there another secret we don't know?

00:08:42.580 --> 00:08:44.870
It's not unlikely.

00:08:44.870 --> 00:08:49.080
"The adults are lying to us."
That's what my brother said.

00:08:49.080 --> 00:08:53.790
There could be some reason why
they can't tell our generation the truth.

00:08:55.620 --> 00:08:58.000
Maybe we should stop here.

00:08:58.000 --> 00:09:01.450
There's no point in arguing
over hypotheses here.

00:09:01.450 --> 00:09:02.790
Aries.

00:09:02.790 --> 00:09:07.290
I'm more concerned about
the atmosphere getting bad.

00:09:07.290 --> 00:09:11.870
Let's make it back to Astra,
see the truth with our own eyes,

00:09:11.870 --> 00:09:15.250
then learn about the things we don't know.

00:09:15.250 --> 00:09:19.750
After all, planetary exploration
is our specialty now, isn't it?

00:09:19.750 --> 00:09:21.750
You're right.

00:09:21.750 --> 00:09:24.580
Let's go home, to Astra.

00:09:28.410 --> 00:09:30.620
Team B5, camp log.

00:09:30.620 --> 00:09:34.040
"In faster-than-light travel
Day 90 of being lost in space"
The <i>Astra </i>is now on its way to
the final planet: Planet Galem.

00:09:34.040 --> 00:09:34.790
The <i>Astra </i>is now on its way to
the final planet: Planet Galem.

00:09:34.790 --> 00:09:37.660
We decided to set aside
the mystery of our world for now,

00:09:37.660 --> 00:09:40.750
and the ship is back to its peaceful state.

00:09:46.700 --> 00:09:49.500
"Let's leave the idiot here
and get to the lodge."

00:09:49.500 --> 00:09:52.290
"Hey guys, what is that?"

00:09:52.290 --> 00:09:53.370
"What is that...?"

00:09:53.370 --> 00:09:55.370
"It's coming closer."

00:09:55.370 --> 00:09:58.580
"Obviously this is just theatrics."

00:09:58.580 --> 00:10:00.950
Whoosh.

00:10:00.950 --> 00:10:03.450
"Everyone, run!"

00:10:13.620 --> 00:10:16.250
Yes, who is it?

00:10:16.250 --> 00:10:18.250
Oh... Kanata.

00:10:18.250 --> 00:10:22.160
Um, what is it? It's lights-out already.

00:10:22.160 --> 00:10:24.540
Aries. I need to talk to you.

00:10:24.540 --> 00:10:29.540
Wait, please! What is it?
I'm not prepared...

00:10:29.540 --> 00:10:31.950
No need to prepare, just let me in.

00:10:32.870 --> 00:10:35.250
No! I mean yes, but no!

00:10:35.250 --> 00:10:37.330
Come on, before someone shows up.

00:10:37.330 --> 00:10:38.620
Why is that a problem?!

00:10:38.620 --> 00:10:40.660
Seriously, seriously. Please, please.
It'll be over super quick.

00:10:40.660 --> 00:10:43.250
Please don't phrase it like that!

00:10:44.540 --> 00:10:47.000
Please, Aries.

00:10:49.370 --> 00:10:51.540
Just talking?

00:10:51.540 --> 00:10:53.080
It's important.

00:10:54.700 --> 00:10:56.500
Okay...

00:11:05.870 --> 00:11:09.450
"Planet Galem
Day 111 of being lost in space"

00:11:09.950 --> 00:11:12.290
We're finally at the last planet.

00:11:12.290 --> 00:11:13.250
Yeah.

00:11:13.250 --> 00:11:15.410
I'm feeling sad, strangely.

00:11:15.410 --> 00:11:18.250
After saying so many times
that you want to go home?

00:11:18.250 --> 00:11:20.700
It was definitely an exciting trip.

00:11:20.700 --> 00:11:22.370
How about you, Aries?

00:11:22.370 --> 00:11:23.910
How was the trip for you?

00:11:23.910 --> 00:11:29.410
Well, a lot happened, but I was
able to complete my goal.

00:11:29.410 --> 00:11:30.910
Goal?

00:11:30.910 --> 00:11:34.120
To become friends with everyone.

00:11:36.250 --> 00:11:39.250
You totally overachieved there.

00:11:43.330 --> 00:11:47.870
Let's start the search in the area
within a 500m radius around the ship.

00:11:47.870 --> 00:11:49.750
Quitterie, stand by in the ship.

00:11:49.750 --> 00:11:51.580
Funi, follow Zack.

00:11:51.580 --> 00:11:52.700
Aye, yeah.

00:11:52.700 --> 00:11:54.290
Charce, how is the atmosphere?

00:11:54.290 --> 00:11:55.950
No problems.

00:11:55.950 --> 00:11:56.910
--Our focus on day one is to gather
a wide variety, not a large quantity.

00:11:56.910 --> 00:11:59.750
--How efficient. Wonderful.
--Our focus on day one is to gather
a wide variety, not a large quantity.

00:11:59.750 --> 00:12:01.290
--This is our fifth time, after all.
--Our focus on day one is to gather
a wide variety, not a large quantity.

00:12:01.290 --> 00:12:03.160
Aye, yeah!

00:12:16.080 --> 00:12:20.750
Impressive! I guess that's another
thing you learned on this trip.

00:12:20.750 --> 00:12:22.120
Yes, looks delicious.

00:12:22.120 --> 00:12:24.910
I'm more impressed by the tastes
you've acquired on this trip...

00:12:25.790 --> 00:12:29.000
This seems like a nice planet,
very lush with nature.

00:12:29.000 --> 00:12:32.750
Yeah, we shouldn't have
much trouble finding food.

00:12:32.750 --> 00:12:35.160
We're really getting home, to Astra.

00:12:35.160 --> 00:12:36.370
Yes.

00:12:39.040 --> 00:12:42.160
I wonder how our lives
will be when we get back.

00:12:42.160 --> 00:12:45.160
I'll probably go back
to living with my mom,

00:12:45.160 --> 00:12:47.500
but the others probably
can't do that, right?

00:12:47.500 --> 00:12:52.290
Yeah. Well, I'm sure the government
would support us until we graduate.

00:12:52.290 --> 00:12:56.160
That said, I'm sure we're all able
to live on our own now.

00:12:56.160 --> 00:13:02.160
After running around the galaxy like this,
what is there to be afraid of anymore?

00:13:02.160 --> 00:13:04.500
I agree.

00:13:04.500 --> 00:13:08.290
I think I grew a bit stronger
during this trip, too.

00:13:08.290 --> 00:13:10.500
Thanks to you.

00:13:13.330 --> 00:13:15.120
When we get home to Astra...

00:13:15.120 --> 00:13:16.500
Yes?

00:13:16.500 --> 00:13:20.290
Um... I, uh, I'll walk you home.

00:13:20.290 --> 00:13:22.120
What?

00:13:22.120 --> 00:13:27.370
A camping trip isn't over until you're
safely home, and I'm the captain.

00:13:27.370 --> 00:13:31.000
Yes, please!
I will introduce you to my mom.

00:13:31.000 --> 00:13:32.830
Um... Okay.

00:13:32.830 --> 00:13:37.750
Right, this area is covered. I'm going to go
take a look in the southern area.

00:13:37.750 --> 00:13:40.450
Aries, go meet up with everyone.
They're in the forest.

00:13:40.450 --> 00:13:43.580
Right, I'll go heat up everyone,
they're in for rest.

00:13:43.580 --> 00:13:45.500
What is it that you're trying to achieve?

00:13:51.500 --> 00:13:53.910
At this rate, it's likely
that we're going to get home.

00:13:53.910 --> 00:13:56.580
The only thing I'm worried about
is the enemy among us.

00:13:56.580 --> 00:14:00.200
Right now, we all share a bond
deeper than friends or companions.

00:14:00.200 --> 00:14:03.330
The enemy probably values this bond, too.

00:14:03.330 --> 00:14:06.370
The fact that they haven't taken
any action against us is proof of this.

00:14:06.370 --> 00:14:11.250
Nobody is trying to figure out who
the killer is precisely because of that bond.

00:14:11.250 --> 00:14:15.040
I don't have to worry about this
if we're going to get home safely.

00:14:15.040 --> 00:14:17.830
We'll just pretend there was
no enemy to begin with...

00:14:25.580 --> 00:14:27.000
It's here...!

00:14:33.370 --> 00:14:36.660
Dammit! Was it a mistake
to go in the cave?!

00:14:42.500 --> 00:14:44.410
Aries!

00:14:44.410 --> 00:14:47.870
Kanata, what's wrong?
Why are you running?

00:14:47.870 --> 00:14:48.910
Aries!

00:14:48.910 --> 00:14:49.910
Sphere...

00:14:49.910 --> 00:14:51.330
What?

00:14:56.250 --> 00:14:57.290
It's gone...

00:14:57.290 --> 00:15:00.120
What happened, Kanata?

00:15:01.500 --> 00:15:03.250
Let's get back to the ship.

00:15:04.580 --> 00:15:08.370
The enemy wants to
kill us all on this planet.

00:15:08.370 --> 00:15:12.660
Then they're planning on getting
home all alone on the <i>Astra</i>.

00:15:12.660 --> 00:15:15.580
I've figured out who the enemy is.

00:15:15.580 --> 00:15:18.870
They don't know that I know.

00:15:18.870 --> 00:15:21.580
I'll make the first move tomorrow.

00:15:21.580 --> 00:15:22.830
It's time for a showdown!

00:15:24.830 --> 00:15:27.660
"Planet Galem
Day 112 of being lost in space"

00:15:28.700 --> 00:15:32.750
Zack, Charce.
I have to talk to you two, alone.

00:15:32.750 --> 00:15:36.120
I was attacked by the sphere yesterday.

00:15:36.120 --> 00:15:37.830
What?!

00:15:37.830 --> 00:15:39.870
Is it the enemy...?

00:15:39.870 --> 00:15:43.830
Yeah, they're trying to kill us all here.

00:15:43.830 --> 00:15:46.620
I'm going to get them before they get us.

00:15:46.620 --> 00:15:49.250
Do you know who it is?

00:15:57.290 --> 00:15:58.410
Ulgar?!

00:15:58.410 --> 00:15:59.290
It can't be!

00:15:59.290 --> 00:16:00.830
Is it Ulgar?!

00:16:00.830 --> 00:16:03.450
Yeah, but I don't have definite proof.

00:16:03.450 --> 00:16:05.910
That's why we're going to entrap him.

00:16:05.910 --> 00:16:08.000
Wait, but why Ulgar?!

00:16:08.000 --> 00:16:13.500
I'll tell you the reason later. We don't
have time for that right now. Just listen.

00:16:13.500 --> 00:16:18.330
That day, the sphere
swallowed us on Planet McPa.

00:16:18.330 --> 00:16:23.160
If the "exit" that we came out of
was used for the exodus,

00:16:23.160 --> 00:16:27.870
why was the "entrance"
on McPa and Vilavurs?

00:16:27.870 --> 00:16:30.750
The enemy is able to carry
the wormhole around.

00:16:30.750 --> 00:16:31.950
Exactly.

00:16:31.950 --> 00:16:35.870
Assuming that's true,
why restart the killing now?

00:16:35.870 --> 00:16:38.040
Doesn't he want to go home to Astra?

00:16:38.040 --> 00:16:41.870
He worked with us this far
to improve his chance of survival.

00:16:41.870 --> 00:16:44.250
But we're close to home now.

00:16:44.250 --> 00:16:47.700
He thinks he can finish the killing
and get home by himself.

00:16:47.700 --> 00:16:51.410
Can't we just lock Ulgar up
and prevent any danger?

00:16:51.410 --> 00:16:55.580
It won't be that easy.
He has two powerful weapons.

00:16:55.580 --> 00:16:56.620
The gun...

00:16:56.620 --> 00:16:58.000
...and the sphere.

00:16:58.000 --> 00:16:59.870
Do you have a plan?

00:16:59.870 --> 00:17:02.200
I tried to anticipate his actions.

00:17:02.200 --> 00:17:04.450
Yesterday, he came after me alone.

00:17:04.450 --> 00:17:07.750
He probably thought it was too risky
to come after all of us at the same time.

00:17:07.750 --> 00:17:09.790
I'm going to take advantage of that.

00:17:09.790 --> 00:17:12.870
Charce, can you go foraging with Ulgar alone?

00:17:12.870 --> 00:17:15.450
You want me to be bait? That's...

00:17:15.450 --> 00:17:16.910
Just hear me out.

00:17:19.620 --> 00:17:24.410
Zack and I will tail you. So try to go
somewhere easy for us to hide...

00:17:24.410 --> 00:17:27.370
That cave to the south, where I
went yesterday. That would be good.

00:17:27.370 --> 00:17:31.200
We'll adjust the helmet communicator
so that only the three of us can hear.

00:17:31.200 --> 00:17:34.250
Then we can adjust our positions
while we lure Ulgar in.

00:17:34.250 --> 00:17:38.410
When he brings out the sphere, we will
jump him from behind and take him down.

00:17:38.410 --> 00:17:40.120
Will it go that easily?

00:17:40.120 --> 00:17:41.580
We have a good chance.

00:17:41.580 --> 00:17:45.540
He thinks he can surprise us,
but we already know what he's up to.

00:17:45.540 --> 00:17:49.080
You just need to watch out for
the moment he brings out the sphere.

00:17:49.080 --> 00:17:55.080
Also, he's tried to attack us with
the sphere three times now and failed.

00:17:55.080 --> 00:17:58.580
He'll probably try to use the gun
this time, to make sure it works.

00:17:58.580 --> 00:18:02.080
I messed with the gun. It shouldn't
be able to fire right away.

00:18:02.080 --> 00:18:06.790
So he should be vulnerable while he's
surprised by the gun malfunction...

00:18:06.790 --> 00:18:07.870
Do you think you can handle it?

00:18:07.870 --> 00:18:10.160
I trust my captain.

00:18:10.160 --> 00:18:11.660
I'm in the cave.

00:18:11.660 --> 00:18:16.700
Go straight down the path. The fluorescent
plants should provide enough light.

00:18:16.700 --> 00:18:18.250
We've arrived as well.

00:18:18.250 --> 00:18:21.660
Try to keep some distance from Ulgar.
Don't get too close.

00:18:32.080 --> 00:18:33.620
We've entered an open area.

00:18:33.620 --> 00:18:37.120
I'll pretend to look for food
and watch Ulgar.

00:18:37.120 --> 00:18:38.620
Charce, abort mission!

00:18:39.410 --> 00:18:40.250
What's wrong?

00:18:40.250 --> 00:18:44.580
It's an emergency!
Quitterie just called. Funi is missing.

00:18:44.580 --> 00:18:45.790
Funi is missing?!

00:18:45.790 --> 00:18:48.040
We all have to look for her!
Head back to the ship!

00:18:48.040 --> 00:18:49.290
Abort the mission!

00:18:49.290 --> 00:18:50.410
Got it.

00:19:17.540 --> 00:19:20.250
Turn off the sphere.

00:19:20.250 --> 00:19:23.370
I knew it was you,

00:19:23.370 --> 00:19:24.700
Charce.

00:19:31.620 --> 00:19:34.200
So this is the device
that controls the sphere...

00:19:34.200 --> 00:19:37.040
What is this, Kanata?

00:19:37.040 --> 00:19:41.000
I saw you bring out the sphere.
I took away the controller device.

00:19:41.000 --> 00:19:44.000
You're the enemy, Charce.

00:19:44.000 --> 00:19:45.660
Why you?!

00:19:47.080 --> 00:19:51.830
Nobody tampered with this gun.
It can shoot whenever I want.

00:19:51.830 --> 00:19:54.200
Ulgar and I are in on this, too.

00:19:57.290 --> 00:20:00.040
So it was all an act... to entrap me.

00:20:00.040 --> 00:20:04.290
Or rather, to entrap the enemy.

00:20:04.290 --> 00:20:06.000
Exactly.

00:20:10.370 --> 00:20:15.910
So I'm the only one
who didn't know? How sad.

00:20:15.910 --> 00:20:21.250
I'm sorry, Charce.
But I... I still believe in you.

00:20:21.250 --> 00:20:24.450
Yeah, Charce! Come on,
this is a mistake, right?!

00:20:24.450 --> 00:20:26.080
Charce!

00:20:27.250 --> 00:20:29.160
How did you know it was me?

00:20:29.160 --> 00:20:30.750
Charce!

00:20:30.750 --> 00:20:35.000
I remembered when we were
running away from the sphere at McPa.

00:20:35.000 --> 00:20:39.950
If the enemy wants to kill all of us,
they need to see it through.

00:20:39.950 --> 00:20:44.160
In other words, the last one
to enter the orb is the enemy.

00:20:44.160 --> 00:20:46.160
And you thought that was me?

00:20:46.160 --> 00:20:51.580
You think, in all that confusion,
you remember who went in the sphere last?

00:20:51.580 --> 00:20:55.370
It's not like you were filming that incident...

00:20:55.370 --> 00:20:56.950
Ah, I see.

00:20:56.950 --> 00:21:01.080
Yes. Aries remembered.

00:21:04.870 --> 00:21:08.500
What were you going to do
if you were wrong?

00:21:08.500 --> 00:21:12.160
Charce, please say it isn't you!

00:21:12.160 --> 00:21:13.830
I'm out of excuses.

00:21:13.830 --> 00:21:15.540
Anything!

00:21:15.540 --> 00:21:22.500
I won't believe you are the enemy.
I wouldn't believe anybody is.

00:21:23.950 --> 00:21:31.160
You were always so kind to me.
You knew so much about biology and cooking.

00:21:31.160 --> 00:21:33.910
You supported everyone all the time.

00:21:33.910 --> 00:21:39.250
If it wasn't for you,
we wouldn't have made it this far.

00:21:39.250 --> 00:21:42.370
So... we're wrong about this, right?

00:21:43.910 --> 00:21:47.870
I... had a mission.

00:21:47.870 --> 00:21:53.660
We are all clones and one of
the originals made you kill us, right?

00:21:53.660 --> 00:21:59.580
Yes. It's like you all said.
This is a cover-up to hide a cloning crime.

00:21:59.580 --> 00:22:02.000
It was supposed to be a simple mission.

00:22:02.000 --> 00:22:09.160
Push the switch on McPa
to send everyone to space.

00:22:09.160 --> 00:22:11.580
I, the culprit, also die.

00:22:11.580 --> 00:22:15.370
It seems like you activated
the sphere too early.

00:22:15.370 --> 00:22:20.370
We were all wearing our crust suits
and we had time to put our helmets on.

00:22:20.370 --> 00:22:27.410
You're right. But I wanted
to do this with my suit on.

00:22:27.410 --> 00:22:32.040
I wanted to die while gazing into space.

00:22:32.040 --> 00:22:33.160
But...

00:22:33.160 --> 00:22:38.250
We somehow found a ship.
That was not part of your plan, was it?

00:22:38.250 --> 00:22:42.160
Yes. After finding the ship
and helping Aries,

00:22:42.160 --> 00:22:45.870
I pretended to investigate
the communicator and disabled it.

00:22:45.870 --> 00:22:48.620
I didn't want you to get in touch.

00:22:48.620 --> 00:22:54.790
But after that, I decided to work
with everyone to get to the last planet.

00:22:54.790 --> 00:22:58.000
And that's how we got here.

00:22:58.000 --> 00:23:02.500
I'm impressed. I really am.

00:23:02.500 --> 00:23:07.910
Who knew working together could allow
people to achieve such greatness?

00:23:07.910 --> 00:23:12.450
Enough! You're the one who tried to kill
all of the people you worked with!

00:23:12.450 --> 00:23:18.000
Charce. Tell us everything.
Why do you have this mission?

00:23:18.000 --> 00:23:24.160
What mission is so important that you
had to kill yourself to achieve it?!

00:23:24.160 --> 00:23:25.450
That's unacceptable!

00:23:25.450 --> 00:23:27.290
Who are you?

00:23:31.790 --> 00:23:34.500
I'm also a clone.

00:23:34.500 --> 00:23:41.000
The only difference is I've known
all along that I am a clone.

00:23:41.000 --> 00:23:43.950
My original is Noah Vix.

00:23:43.950 --> 00:23:46.660
The ruler of the Vixia Royal Quarter.

00:23:46.660 --> 00:23:48.500
I am a clone of the king.
